    title: "Constant-Time Insert, Delete and Inspect",
    topic: "arrays-hashing",
    difficulty: "Medium",
    pattern: "hash map from value to slot / swap-with-last removal",
    statement: "A container holds distinct integers in a sequence that starts out empty. You are given a stream of instructions, one per cell of `ops`:\n\n- a positive cell `v` inserts the value `v` at the end of the sequence, unless `v` is already in it;\n- a negative cell `v` deletes the value `-v` if it is present, by the swap-with-last rule: the freed slot is overwritten with the last element of the sequence, and the sequence then loses its final slot;\n- a cell equal to `0` does nothing.\n\nDeleting a value that is not in the sequence changes nothing at all.\n\nReturn the sequence that remains once every instruction has been applied, in its final order.\n\nFor example, with `ops = [3, 1, 2, -3]` the sequence runs `[3]`, `[3, 1]`, `[3, 1, 2]`, and the final delete moves the `2` into the slot the `3` occupied, giving `[2, 1]`.\n\nConstraints: `1 <= ops.length <= 200` and `-50 <= ops[i] <= 50`.\n",
    examples: [
      { input: "ops = [-50]", output: "[]", explanation: "Produced by the reference solution, verified against all four implementations." },
      { input: "ops = [-3, 47, -30, 19, 49]", output: "[47, 19, 49]", explanation: "Produced by the reference solution, verified against all four implementations." },
    ],
    constraints: ["Function signature: `function solve(ops: number[])`.", "Inputs are JSON-serializable values satisfying the bounds stated above."],
    hints: [
      "The returned sequence is the only thing the caller sees, but the work is deciding quickly whether a value is already in it.",
      "Deletion does not need to preserve order: the rule lets you drop the last element into the hole and shrink the sequence by one slot.",
      "Keep a second structure mapping each stored value to the slot it currently sits in, and remember to move the entry of the value you shifted into the hole.",
    ],
    solutions: [
      {
        title: "Brute Force",
        complexity: "Time: O(n²) | Space: O(n)",
        language: "javascript",
        code: "function solve(ops) {\n  const seq = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < ops.length; i++) {\n    const step = ops[i];\n    if (step > 0) {\n      if (seq.indexOf(step) === -1) seq.push(step);\n    } else if (step < 0) {\n      const at = seq.indexOf(-step);\n      if (at !== -1) {\n        seq[at] = seq[seq.length - 1];\n        seq.pop();\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return seq;\n}",
      },
      {
        title: "Optimal",
        complexity: "Time: O(n) | Space: O(n)",
        language: "javascript",
        code: "function solve(ops) {\n  const slot = new Map();\n  const seq = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < ops.length; i++) {\n    const step = ops[i];\n    if (step > 0) {\n      if (!slot.has(step)) {\n        slot.set(step, seq.length);\n        seq.push(step);\n      }\n    } else if (step < 0) {\n      const target = -step;\n      if (slot.has(target)) {\n        const at = slot.get(target);\n        const moved = seq[seq.length - 1];\n        seq[at] = moved;\n        slot.set(moved, at);\n        seq.pop();\n        slot.delete(target);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return seq;\n}",
      },
    ],
