    id: "heap-6",
    slug: "find-median-from-data-stream",
    title: "Find Median from Data Stream",
    topic: "heap",
    difficulty: "Hard",
    pattern: "heap / two-heap running median",
    statement: "A sensor reports readings one at a time as the elements of nums. Right after each reading arrives, the sensor records the running median of the readings seen so far, using the lower median whenever the count is even: for a sorted list of m readings the lower median is the element at index (m - 1) // 2, counting from zero. The first reading therefore contributes its own value.\n\nReturn the sum of the running medians recorded over all prefixes of nums.\n\nFor example, nums = [1, 2, 3, 4] gives the running medians 1, 1, 2 and 2, so the answer is 6.\n\nConstraints: `1 <= nums.length <= 200` and `-10000 <= nums[i] <= 10000`.\n",
    examples: [
      { input: "nums = [-10000]", output: "-10000", explanation: "Produced by the reference solution, verified against all four implementations." },
      { input: "nums = [-221, 6635, 9954, -3483]", output: "5972", explanation: "Produced by the reference solution, verified against all four implementations." },
    ],
    constraints: ["Function signature: `function solve(nums: number[])`.", "Inputs are JSON-serializable values satisfying the bounds stated above."],
    hints: [
      "You need the middle value after each insertion, and the middle value depends only on how the readings split into a smaller half and a larger half.",
      "Keep the smaller half in a max-heap and the larger half in a min-heap, and keep their sizes within one of each other.",
      "Define the median as the element at index (m - 1) // 2 of the sorted prefix; then the answer is the top of the max-heap after each balancing move, accumulated over all prefixes.",
    ],
    solutions: [
      {
        title: "Brute Force",
        complexity: "Time: O(n * n log n) | Space: O(n)",
        language: "javascript",
        code: "function solve(nums) {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\n    const window = nums.slice(0, i + 1).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n    total += window[Math.floor((window.length - 1) / 2)];\n  }\n  return total;\n}",
      },
      {
        title: "Optimal",
        complexity: "Time: O(n log n) | Space: O(n)",
        language: "javascript",
        code: "function solve(nums) {\n  const low = [];\n  const high = [];\n  function pushLow(v) {\n    low.push(v);\n    let i = low.length - 1;\n    while (i > 0) {\n      const p = (i - 1) >> 1;\n      if (low[p] >= low[i]) break;\n      const t = low[p];\n      low[p] = low[i];\n      low[i] = t;\n      i = p;\n    }\n  }\n  function popLow() {\n    const top = low[0];\n    const last = low.pop();\n    if (low.length > 0) {\n      low[0] = last;\n      let i = 0;\n      while (true) {\n        const l = 2 * i + 1;\n        const r = 2 * i + 2;\n        let m = i;\n        if (l < low.length && low[l] > low[m]) m = l;\n        if (r < low.length && low[r] > low[m]) m = r;\n        if (m === i) break;\n        const t = low[m];\n        low[m] = low[i];\n        low[i] = t;\n        i = m;\n      }\n    }\n    return top;\n  }\n  function pushHigh(v) {\n    high.push(v);\n    let i = high.length - 1;\n    while (i > 0) {\n      const p = (i - 1) >> 1;\n      if (high[p] <= high[i]) break;\n      const t = high[p];\n      high[p] = high[i];\n      high[i] = t;\n      i = p;\n    }\n  }\n  function popHigh() {\n    const top = high[0];\n    const last = high.pop();\n    if (high.length > 0) {\n      high[0] = last;\n      let i = 0;\n      while (true) {\n        const l = 2 * i + 1;\n        const r = 2 * i + 2;\n        let m = i;\n        if (l < high.length && high[l] < high[m]) m = l;\n        if (r < high.length && high[r] < high[m]) m = r;\n        if (m === i) break;\n        const t = high[m];\n        high[m] = high[i];\n        high[i] = t;\n        i = m;\n      }\n    }\n    return top;\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const x of nums) {\n    if (low.length === 0 || x <= low[0]) pushLow(x);\n    else pushHigh(x);\n    if (low.length > high.length + 1) pushHigh(popLow());\n    else if (high.length > low.length) pushLow(popHigh());\n    total += low[0];\n  }\n  return total;\n}",
      },
    ],
