    constraints: ["Function signature: `function solve(startTime: number[], endTime: number[], profit: number[])`.", "Inputs are JSON-serializable values satisfying the bounds stated above."],
    hints: [
      "The three arrays are read in parallel, so the number of contracts is the length of the shortest of them, and each contract spans the interval between its two moments in whichever order they arrive, so normalise every pair with `min` and `max` first.",
      "A span may follow another only when it begins no earlier than the first one finishes. Sort the contracts by finish and any valid selection then walks forward through that order, so the contract chosen before the current one always comes earlier.",
      "Define `dp[i]` as the best pay using only the first `i` contracts in finish order. For contract `i` you either skip it and keep `dp[i-1]`, or take it and add `profit[i]` to the best schedule that finishes no later than its begin. That predecessor is the last contract with `finish <= begin`, and because the array is sorted by finish it is a lower-bound query: binary search it and use `dp[j] + profit[i]`. `dp[0] = 0` covers taking nothing.",
    ],
    solutions: [
      {
        title: "Brute Force",
        complexity: "Time: O(n²) | Space: O(n)",
        language: "javascript",
        code: "function solve(startTime, endTime, profit) {\n  const n = Math.min(startTime.length, endTime.length, profit.length);\n  const jobs = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    const begin = Math.min(startTime[i], endTime[i]);\n    const finish = Math.max(startTime[i], endTime[i]);\n    jobs.push([finish, begin, i, profit[i]]);\n  }\n  jobs.sort((a, b) => (a[0] - b[0]) || (a[1] - b[1]) || (a[2] - b[2]));\n  const dp = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);\n  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n    const begin = jobs[i - 1][1];\n    const pay = jobs[i - 1][3];\n    let j = i - 1;\n    while (j > 0 && jobs[j - 1][0] > begin) j--;\n    const take = dp[j] + pay;\n    dp[i] = take > dp[i - 1] ? take : dp[i - 1];\n  }\n  return dp[n];\n}",
      },
      {
        title: "Optimal",
        complexity: "Time: O(n log n) | Space: O(n)",
        language: "javascript",
        code: "function solve(startTime, endTime, profit) {\n  const n = Math.min(startTime.length, endTime.length, profit.length);\n  const jobs = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    const begin = Math.min(startTime[i], endTime[i]);\n    const finish = Math.max(startTime[i], endTime[i]);\n    jobs.push([finish, begin, i, profit[i]]);\n  }\n  jobs.sort((a, b) => (a[0] - b[0]) || (a[1] - b[1]) || (a[2] - b[2]));\n  const ends = jobs.map((job) => job[0]);\n  const dp = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);\n  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n    const begin = jobs[i - 1][1];\n    const pay = jobs[i - 1][3];\n    let lo = 0;\n    let hi = i - 1;\n    while (lo < hi) {\n      const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi + 1) / 2);\n      if (ends[mid - 1] <= begin) lo = mid;\n      else hi = mid - 1;\n    }\n    const take = dp[lo] + pay;\n    dp[i] = take > dp[i - 1] ? take : dp[i - 1];\n  }\n  return dp[n];\n}",
      },
    ],
