    title: "Design In-Memory File System",
    topic: "trie",
    difficulty: "Hard",
    pattern: "design / trie of path segments",
    statement: "A log records paths that were created in an in-memory file system, and you replay it in order. Each element of paths names one node that was created. A path that ends with a slash marks a directory, any other path marks a file, and a path with no name segments at all, such as \"/\", is ignored. Every path is read as absolute, so a leading slash carries no extra meaning and repeated slashes act as a single separator. A path like '/a/b/c.txt' also creates the directories /a and /a/b when they do not exist yet. An element is ignored when a name already exists as a file, when the element would turn an existing file into a directory, or when it would turn an existing directory into a file.\n\nAfter every element has been applied, report the immediate children of the directory target as a single string. Each child contributes its own name, followed by a slash when that child is a directory, and the entries are sorted in plain ascending order of the name alone, decided before the slash is appended. Join the entries with newline characters and return the empty string when target does not name an existing directory. A target with no name segments refers to the root directory.\n\nFor example, for paths = ['/a/', '/a/b.txt'] and target = '/', the answer is 'a/'.\n\nConstraints: `1 <= paths.length <= 150` and `1 <= paths[i].length <= 40` and `0 <= target.length <= 40`.\n",
    examples: [
      { input: "paths = [\"h\"], target = \"r\"", output: "\"\"", explanation: "Produced by the reference solution, verified against all four implementations." },
      { input: "paths = [\"tzr6852f-c1u-qb\", \"o._\", \"r\", \"cl472rl_15f4w0vugkv\"], target = \"5sz9c3fuquhz6a\"", output: "\"\"", explanation: "Produced by the reference solution, verified against all four implementations." },
    ],
    constraints: ["Function signature: `function solve(paths: string[], target: string)`.", "Inputs are JSON-serializable values satisfying the bounds stated above."],
    hints: [
      "Every path is a walk from the root; the only state you need per node is whether it is a directory and which names live directly under it.",
      "Insert one segment at a time, creating missing segments as directories, but check the whole path first because a segment that already exists as a file makes the entry invalid.",
      "For the listing, gather the immediate children of the queried node, sort the bare names, and only then add a trailing slash to the directories.",
    ],
    solutions: [
      {
        title: "Brute Force",
        complexity: "Time: O(n * d * d + n log n) | Space: O(n * d)",
        language: "javascript",
        code: "function solve(paths, target) {\n  const kind = Object.create(null);\n  function segments(text) {\n    if (typeof text !== 'string') return null;\n    const parts = text.split('/');\n    const out = [];\n    for (const part of parts) {\n      if (part.length > 0) out.push(part);\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n  function keyOf(segs) {\n    return '/' + segs.join('/');\n  }\n  for (const raw of paths) {\n    const segs = segments(raw);\n    if (segs === null || segs.length === 0) continue;\n    const wantDir = raw.charAt(raw.length - 1) === '/';\n    let ok = true;\n    for (let i = 0; i < segs.length; i++) {\n      const existing = kind[keyOf(segs.slice(0, i + 1))];\n      if (existing === undefined) break;\n      const isLast = i === segs.length - 1;\n      if (isLast ? existing !== wantDir : existing !== true) {\n        ok = false;\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n    if (!ok) continue;\n    for (let i = 0; i < segs.length; i++) {\n      const k = keyOf(segs.slice(0, i + 1));\n      if (kind[k] === undefined) {\n        kind[k] = i === segs.length - 1 ? wantDir : true;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  const q = segments(target);\n  if (q === null) return '';\n  const prefix = q.length === 0 ? '/' : keyOf(q) + '/';\n  if (q.length > 0 && kind[keyOf(q)] !== true) return '';\n  const seen = Object.create(null);\n  const names = [];\n  for (const k of Object.keys(kind)) {\n    if (k.indexOf(prefix) !== 0) continue;\n    const rest = k.slice(prefix.length);\n    if (rest.length === 0) continue;\n    const cut = rest.indexOf('/');\n    const name = cut === -1 ? rest : rest.slice(0, cut);\n    if (seen[name] === true) continue;\n    seen[name] = true;\n    names.push(name);\n  }\n  names.sort();\n  const out = [];\n  for (const name of names) {\n    out.push(kind[prefix + name] === true ? name + '/' : name);\n  }\n  return out.join('\\n');\n}",
      },
      {
        title: "Optimal",
        complexity: "Time: O(n * d + m log m) | Space: O(n * d)",
        language: "javascript",
        code: "function solve(paths, target) {\n  function segments(text) {\n    if (typeof text !== 'string') return null;\n    const parts = text.split('/');\n    const out = [];\n    for (const part of parts) {\n      if (part.length > 0) out.push(part);\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n  const root = { isDir: true, kids: new Map() };\n  for (const raw of paths) {\n    const segs = segments(raw);\n    if (segs === null || segs.length === 0) continue;\n    const wantDir = raw.charAt(raw.length - 1) === '/';\n    let ok = true;\n    let walker = root;\n    for (let i = 0; i < segs.length; i++) {\n      const nxt = walker.kids.get(segs[i]);\n      if (nxt === undefined) break;\n      const isLast = i === segs.length - 1;\n      if (isLast ? nxt.isDir !== wantDir : !nxt.isDir) {\n        ok = false;\n        break;\n      }\n      walker = nxt;\n    }\n    if (!ok) continue;\n    let node = root;\n    for (let i = 0; i < segs.length; i++) {\n      const isLast = i === segs.length - 1;\n      let child = node.kids.get(segs[i]);\n      if (child === undefined) {\n        child = { isDir: isLast ? wantDir : true, kids: new Map() };\n        node.kids.set(segs[i], child);\n      }\n      node = child;\n    }\n  }\n  const q = segments(target);\n  if (q === null) return '';\n  let node = root;\n  for (const seg of q) {\n    const child = node.kids.get(seg);\n    if (child === undefined || !child.isDir) return '';\n    node = child;\n  }\n  const names = [];\n  for (const name of node.kids.keys()) names.push(name);\n  names.sort();\n  const out = [];\n  for (const name of names) {\n    out.push(node.kids.get(name).isDir ? name + '/' : name);\n  }\n  return out.join('\\n');\n}",
      },
    ],
